35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the treasurer spent six hours a month chasing individual payments, but only one for yearly collections. That is a huge difference.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger confirms seventy percent of costs are fixed, regardless of attendance. The treasurer’s logs show yearly collection is far more efficient. We must avoid per-event chasing.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, the fixed costs confirm your point. But the sign-in sheets show a quarter of members do two-thirds of the work, while eighteen never appear.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Minako, that imbalance is real, but my data shows the hesitation is about commitment. People won’t sign up for a whole year at once.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, the data is undeniable. The same nine people do the setup and locking up. @May, the quiet members are anxious about the per-event cost.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, that makes sense. If yearly collection is easier, maybe we should just do that? I don’t want the next person to be so tired.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, efficiency is necessary, but not sufficient. We must ensure the fee covers the fixed costs without overburdening those who attend less.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, efficiency is vital, but the taster forms show people fear a full-year commitment. We need a structure that respects that hesitation while covering the fixed costs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, exactly. The data proves it. People freeze when asked to commit to a whole year upfront. We need a way in that feels lighter.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, the fear of commitment is real, but the data shows the heavy users are already carrying the load. We need a structure that acknowledges that reality, not just the hesitation.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, I agree. But if we charge everyone the same, the quiet members might feel it is unfair. How do we balance that?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, a flat fee ignores the attendance gap. We need a structure that reflects actual usage, not just fixed costs.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, a flat fee ignores the hesitation. @Shunichi, tiers risk the friction we saw before. We need a middle path that respects both the fixed costs and the newcomers’ fear of commitment.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
